==Old English==

===Etymology===
From earlier {{m|ang|æces}} (compare also Northumbrian {{m|ang|acas}}), from {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{m|gem-pro|*akwisī}}, probably from a {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₂egʷs-ih₂-||axe}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₂eḱ-||sharp, pointed}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|axa}}, {{cog|osx|akus}} ({{cog|nds|Ax}}, {{m|nds|Äx}}, {{m|nds|Ex}}), {{cog|nl|aaks}}, {{cog|goh|ackus}} ({{cog|de|Axt}}), {{cog|non|øx}} ({{cog|da|økse}}, {{cog|sv|yxa}}), {{cog|got|𐌰𐌵𐌹𐌶𐌹}}.

